{# A voice in another language than the subtitle (Entity.yaml spoken_language, per NPC): the model writes
   each spoken sentence as usual and, right after it, the voice's words in a block named by the language's
   code, `Come in. <ja>入って。</ja>`. SkyrimNet pairs a sentence with its block and voices the words; the
   subtitle, the event history and what other NPCs hear keep the sentence as written. A sentence without a
   block is spoken as written. decnpc(uuid).spokenLanguage is {code, name}, or nothing. The sentence's own
   language is never named: players who prompt for another language keep it, and only the block changes. #}
{% if render_mode == "full" and decnpc(npc.UUID).spokenLanguage %}
{% set _sl = decnpc(npc.UUID).spokenLanguage %}
{% set _name = decnpc(npc.UUID).name %}
{% set _ex1 = "" %}
{% set _ex2 = "" %}
{% if _sl.code == "ja" %}{% set _ex1 = "今はだめ。" %}{% set _ex2 = "一時間後にまた来て。" %}
{% else if _sl.code == "ko" %}{% set _ex1 = "지금은 안 돼." %}{% set _ex2 = "한 시간 뒤에 다시 와." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "zh" %}{% set _ex1 = "现在不行。" %}{% set _ex2 = "一个小时后再来。" %}
{% else if _sl.code == "ru" %}{% set _ex1 = "Не сейчас." %}{% set _ex2 = "Возвращайся через час." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "it" %}{% set _ex1 = "Non ora." %}{% set _ex2 = "Torna tra un'ora." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "es" %}{% set _ex1 = "Ahora no." %}{% set _ex2 = "Vuelve dentro de una hora." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "pt" %}{% set _ex1 = "Agora não." %}{% set _ex2 = "Volte daqui a uma hora." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "de" %}{% set _ex1 = "Jetzt nicht." %}{% set _ex2 = "Komm in einer Stunde wieder." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "fr" %}{% set _ex1 = "Pas maintenant." %}{% set _ex2 = "Reviens dans une heure." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "ar" %}{% set _ex1 = "ليس الآن." %}{% set _ex2 = "ارجع بعد ساعة." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "pl" %}{% set _ex1 = "Nie teraz." %}{% set _ex2 = "Wróć za godzinę." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "nl" %}{% set _ex1 = "Nu niet." %}{% set _ex2 = "Kom over een uur terug." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "hi" %}{% set _ex1 = "अभी नहीं।" %}{% set _ex2 = "एक घंटे बाद वापस आना।" %}
{% else if _sl.code == "he" %}{% set _ex1 = "לא עכשיו." %}{% set _ex2 = "תחזור בעוד שעה." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "cs" %}{% set _ex1 = "Teď ne." %}{% set _ex2 = "Vrať se za hodinu." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "hu" %}{% set _ex1 = "Most nem." %}{% set _ex2 = "Gyere vissza egy óra múlva." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "tr" %}{% set _ex1 = "Şimdi değil." %}{% set _ex2 = "Bir saat sonra tekrar gel." %}
{% else if _sl.code == "en" %}{% set _ex1 = "Not now." %}{% set _ex2 = "Come back in an hour." %}
{% endif %}
## Spoken Language
{{ _name }} speaks {{ _sl.name }} aloud, while the subtitles stay in the language of this conversation. Write each spoken sentence as you normally would and, right after it, inside <{{ _sl.code }}>...</{{ _sl.code }}>, the natural spoken {{ _sl.name }} that {{ _name }} actually says: the same meaning and about the same length, in {{ _name }}'s personality and register, using the established {{ _sl.name }} localization of Elder Scrolls names and terms.
- One <{{ _sl.code }}> block directly after each spoken sentence, the last one included: a sentence without its block is a mistake. Never put the {{ _sl.name }} first, never group several sentences into one block.
{% if is_audio_tags_enabled(npc.UUID) %}
- Keep [performance tags] in the sentence itself; do not repeat them inside the block.
{% endif %}
- Narration in *asterisks*, <internal_thought> blocks and ACTION lines stay as they are, with no block.
{% if length(_ex1) > 0 %}
- Example, for a conversation written in English: Not now. <{{ _sl.code }}>{{ _ex1 }}</{{ _sl.code }}>{% if is_narration_enabled() %} *{{ _name }} does not look up*{% endif %} Come back in an hour. <{{ _sl.code }}>{{ _ex2 }}</{{ _sl.code }}>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
